1
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:11,039
Japan is an island nation with a fleet built for distance.

2
00:00:11,039 --> 00:00:17,391
Here is every aircraft its military is flying in 2026 — the fighters, the gunships,

3
00:00:17,391 --> 00:00:21,983
the patrol planes, the tankers, the trainers and the drones.

4
00:00:23,233 --> 00:00:28,516
Japan is an island nation, and its air force is built to cover open sea,

5
00:00:28,516 --> 00:00:31,597
far-flung islands and very long distances.

6
00:00:31,597 --> 00:00:33,358
Start with the fighters.

7
00:00:33,358 --> 00:00:39,081
Two hundred F-15J Eagles still form the backbone, licence-built by Mitsubishi,

8
00:00:39,081 --> 00:00:44,730
meeting Chinese and Russian aircraft near Japanese airspace almost every day.

9
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:49,426
The F-2 is the anti-ship striker: a larger wing, heavy missiles,

10
00:00:49,426 --> 00:00:53,094
designed to break up a landing fleet far offshore.

11
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:59,183
And the F-35 quietly changes the maths — one of the largest fleets outside America,

12
00:00:59,183 --> 00:01:05,273
with the short-takeoff B models destined for the converted carriers Izumo and Kaga.

13
00:01:06,073 --> 00:01:10,956
Attack helicopters are the part of the fleet Japan is letting go.

14
00:01:10,956 --> 00:01:14,787
The AH-1S Cobra was the ground force's tank killer,

15
00:01:14,787 --> 00:01:21,322
bought to blunt a Soviet landing on Hokkaido; only thirty-four were left in March 2026.

16
00:01:21,322 --> 00:01:26,430
The AH-64D Apache was meant to be the heavy fist — twelve were kept,

17
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:30,862
after costs soared and licence production was halted early.

18
00:01:30,862 --> 00:01:35,369
Both were built for a fight that drones now do more cheaply,

19
00:01:35,369 --> 00:01:40,102
and Japan has already started retiring the units that fly them.

20
00:01:40,902 --> 00:01:42,444
Then the workhorses.

21
00:01:42,444 --> 00:01:49,155
The CH-47J Chinook has been Japan's heavy lifter since nineteen eighty-six — artillery,

22
00:01:49,155 --> 00:01:55,789
troops, relief supplies, and in twenty eleven, water dropped on the crippled Fukushima

23
00:01:55,789 --> 00:01:56,483
reactors.

24
00:01:56,483 --> 00:02:02,345
The SH-60K Seahawk hunts submarines from destroyers and helicopter carriers,

25
00:02:02,345 --> 00:02:06,433
lowering a dipping sonar into the water around Japan.

26
00:02:06,433 --> 00:02:20,472
And the V-22 Osprey finally left its temporary base: by August 2025 the whole fleet had moved to Camp Saga in Kyushu, close to the amphibious brigade it was bought to carry along the

27
00:02:20,472 --> 00:02:22,477
southwestern island chain.

28
00:02:23,277 --> 00:02:29,365
Out over the sea lanes, Japan flies some of the longest patrol missions in the world.

29
00:02:29,365 --> 00:02:33,735
The P-3C Orion hunted Soviet submarines through the Cold War;

30
00:02:33,735 --> 00:02:37,603
only twenty-four remain as a homegrown jet takes over.

31
00:02:37,603 --> 00:02:42,402
The Kawasaki P-1 is that jet — four engines, fly-by-light controls,

32
00:02:42,402 --> 00:02:47,201
and the first patrol aircraft designed and built entirely in Japan.

33
00:02:47,201 --> 00:02:53,647
Forty were in service in March 2026, though spare-parts shortages have reportedly grounded

34
00:02:53,647 --> 00:02:54,578
some of them.

35
00:02:54,578 --> 00:02:58,876
Between them, these two types watch the water between Japan,

36
00:02:58,876 --> 00:03:01,311
its islands and the wider Pacific.

37
00:03:02,111 --> 00:03:09,628
To move troops, fuel and cargo across a very long country, Japan relies on the airlift wing.

38
00:03:09,628 --> 00:03:12,814
The C-2 is the homegrown jet airlifter,

39
00:03:12,814 --> 00:03:18,615
designed by Kawasaki to carry heavy vehicles between scattered islands.

40
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:22,618
The C-130H has served since nineteen eighty-four,

41
00:03:22,618 --> 00:03:26,622
and some now refuel rescue helicopters in flight.

42
00:03:26,622 --> 00:03:41,492
Around them sit the tankers: the KC-767, Japan's first, which quietly gave the force a reach it had never had, and the newer KC-46A Pegasus, whose camera-guided boom has had teething

43
00:03:41,492 --> 00:03:43,861
problems in American service.

44
00:03:44,661 --> 00:03:49,883
Some of the most important aircraft in the fleet carry no weapons at all.

45
00:03:49,883 --> 00:04:02,690
Four E-767s lift a radar dome high over the horizon and turn the air force into a single network: every fighter, every ship, every rescue helicopter seeing what the aircraft above

46
00:04:02,690 --> 00:04:03,620
them can see.

47
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:08,127
The E-2D Advanced Hawkeye does the same job from smaller decks,

48
00:04:08,127 --> 00:04:11,632
watching the water between Japan and its islands.

49
00:04:11,632 --> 00:04:16,426
Neither type fires a shot, and both decide how the fight is fought.

50
00:04:17,226 --> 00:04:20,424
Not every aircraft in the fleet is built to fight.

51
00:04:20,424 --> 00:04:23,814
The T-4 has trained Japanese pilots for four decades,

52
00:04:23,814 --> 00:04:27,780
and still does the job at a fraction of the cost of a fighter.

53
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:33,473
The US-2 flying boat is the strange one: it lands on open ocean to pull people out of the

54
00:04:33,473 --> 00:04:38,782
sea, and a transport version flies supplies to Japan's research base in Antarctica.

55
00:04:38,782 --> 00:04:44,474
Both are reminders that a military fleet is mostly made of everything that is not combat.

56
00:04:45,274 --> 00:04:46,843
Last, the newest wing.

57
00:04:46,843 --> 00:04:53,188
The RQ-4B Global Hawk flies higher and stays up longer than anything with a pilot aboard,

58
00:04:53,188 --> 00:04:56,253
watching the sea lanes for hours at a time.

59
00:04:56,253 --> 00:05:01,172
It is a small fleet doing a big job — the same job the P-3C once did,

60
00:05:01,172 --> 00:05:06,163
and the same job drones are now taking from Japan's retiring gunships.

61
00:05:06,163 --> 00:05:11,153
That is the shape of the fleet in 2026: fewer airframes, longer reach,

62
00:05:11,153 --> 00:05:15,716
and more of the work done by aircraft that never carry a person.

